---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BirdNET-Edge · Arjun Basandrai"
  description="On-device bioacoustic classifier identifying 1,400+ bird species at under 40ms latency on a Raspberry Pi."
  current="projects"
>
  <main>
    <section class="proj-hero wrap">
      <div class="crumb"><a href="/projects">Projects</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Applied ML</div>
      <span class="badge is-active"><span class="dot"></span> Active · 2025–present</span>
      <h1>BirdNET-Edge</h1>
      <p class="summary">Identifying 1,400+ bird species from raw audio, in real time, on a $35 computer with no internet.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href="#">View on GitHub ↗</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#">Live demo ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="ph proj-cover"><span>cover, field station at dawn</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap" style="padding-bottom:8px;">
      <dl class="meta-strip">
        <div class="m"><dt>Role</dt><dd>Solo, research & build</dd></div>
        <div class="m"><dt>Timeline</dt><dd>8 months</dd></div>
        <div class="m"><dt>Stack</dt><dd>PyTorch · ONNX · C++</dd></div>
        <div class="m"><dt>Status</dt><dd>Deployed at 6 sites</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section--tight wrap">
      <div class="case">
        <nav class="case-toc" data-toc aria-label="Sections">
          <h4>In this project</h4>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#problem" class="active">Problem</a></li>
            <li><a href="#motivation">Motivation</a></li>
            <li><a href="#approach">Approach</a></li>
            <li><a href="#architecture">Architecture</a></li>
            <li><a href="#results">Results</a></li>
            <li><a href="#challenges">Challenges</a></li>
            <li><a href="#learnings">Learnings</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <div class="case-body">
          <section id="problem">
            <h2><span class="num">01</span> The problem</h2>
            <p>Conservation field stations want to monitor bird populations continuously, but the places that matter most, like wetlands, remote forest, and island reserves, rarely have power or connectivity. Cloud-based audio classification is a non-starter when you can't reach the cloud, and shipping raw audio off-site is both expensive and slow.</p>
            <p>The goal was a classifier that runs <strong>entirely on-device</strong>, in real time, on hardware cheap enough to deploy by the dozen and rugged enough to leave in a swamp for a season.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="motivation">
            <h2><span class="num">02</span> Motivation</h2>
            <p>I'd been birding by ear for years, and I kept thinking about how much information is in a dawn chorus that no human can fully transcribe. Existing models were accurate but heavy: hundreds of megabytes, hundreds of milliseconds per inference. None of them fit the constraint that actually mattered: a Raspberry Pi, a USB mic, and a solar panel.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="approach">
            <h2><span class="num">03</span> Approach</h2>
            <p>I started from a strong teacher model and worked backwards toward the edge. The pipeline turns a rolling 3-second audio window into a mel-spectrogram, runs a compact CNN, and aggregates predictions over time to suppress spurious single-frame detections.</p>
            <h3>Getting it small</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Knowledge distillation</strong> from a large teacher into a MobileNet-style student.</li>
              <li><strong>Post-training quantization</strong> to int8, with per-channel scales for the first conv block.</li>
              <li><strong>Class-balanced fine-tuning</strong> so rare species didn't get crushed by common ones.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="callout">
              <svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v4l2.5 2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              <p><strong>Key decision</strong>The rare species are the whole point of conservation monitoring. I weighted the loss so a missed warbler hurt far more than a missed pigeon. Accuracy went down on paper, value went up in the field.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="architecture">
            <h2><span class="num">04</span> Architecture</h2>
            <p>The on-device path is deliberately boring, because predictable latency beats peak throughput when you're running on a battery.</p>
            <div class="arch">
              <div class="step"><div class="k">in</div><div class="t">Mic → 3s rolling buffer</div></div>
              <div class="step"><div class="k">pre</div><div class="t">Mel-spectrogram (C++)</div></div>
              <div class="step"><div class="k">model</div><div class="t">int8 CNN via ONNX Runtime</div></div>
              <div class="step"><div class="k">out</div><div class="t">Temporal smoothing → log</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure>
              <div class="ph"><span>architecture diagram</span></div>
              <figcaption>Fig. 1: End-to-end inference path, entirely on the Raspberry Pi.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </section>

          <section id="results">
            <h2><span class="num">05</span> Results</h2>
            <p>After distillation and quantization, the model held its accuracy while shrinking dramatically and dropping under the real-time latency bar.</p>
            <div class="results">
              <div class="r"><b>38ms</b><span>per inference on a Pi 4</span><small>↓ from 410ms</small></div>
              <div class="r"><b>11×</b><span>smaller on disk</span><small>312MB → 28MB</small></div>
              <div class="r"><b>0.91</b><span>macro-F1, 1,400 classes</span><small>−0.02 vs teacher</small></div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="challenges">
            <h2><span class="num">06</span> Challenges</h2>
            <p>Quantization is where the bodies are buried. The mel-spectrogram front-end was numerically sensitive, and naive int8 quantization wiped out quiet, distant calls — exactly the ones field ecologists care about. Keeping the first block in higher precision recovered most of the loss.</p>
            <p>The other surprise was <strong>wind</strong>. Field recordings are nothing like the training set, so I had to build an augmentation pipeline from real ambient recordings to stop the model hallucinating ducks in every gust.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="learnings">
            <h2><span class="num">07</span> Learnings</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>The deployment constraint should drive the model, not the other way around.</li>
              <li>Domain experts know which errors are expensive — ask them before you pick a metric.</li>
              <li>For edge ML, the front-end preprocessing is as important as the network and gets a fraction of the attention.</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="next-proj">
      <a class="wrap np-inner" href="/projects/birdnet-edge">
        <div><div class="k">Next project →</div><div class="t">Sparse Routing for Long-Context Retrieval</div></div>
        <span class="feat-go" style="width:52px;height:52px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .proj-hero { padding-top: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .crumb { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .crumb a:hover { color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .proj-hero h1 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6.5vw, 5rem); line-height: 0.98; letter-spacing: -0.022em; margin: 14px 0; }
  .proj-hero .summary { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.2vw, 1.6rem); color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 50ch; line-height: 1.4; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .proj-cover { aspect-ratio: 21/8; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: var(--radius); }

  /* meta strip */
  .meta-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--line); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; }
  .meta-strip .m { background: var(--surface); padding: 22px 24px; }
  .meta-strip dt { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .meta-strip dd { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 15px; }

  .case { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr minmax(0,700px) 1fr; gap: 40px; }
  .case-body { grid-column: 2; }
  .case-body section { margin-top: 3em; scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .case-body h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin-bottom: 1em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; }
  .case-body h2 .num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .case-body h3 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 1.6em 0 0.6em; }
  .case-body p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .case-body p + p { margin-top: 1.2em; }
  .case-body ul { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .case-body li { margin: 0.5em 0; }
  .case-body strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  .case-toc { grid-column: 1; position: sticky; top: 90px; align-self: start; font-size: 13.5px; padding-right: 24px; }
  .case-toc h4 { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px; font-weight: 400; }
  .case-toc ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .case-toc a { display: block; padding: 5px 0 5px 16px; margin-left: -1px; border-left: 2px solid transparent; color: var(--muted); transition: all .2s; }
  .case-toc a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .case-toc a.active { color: var(--accent-ink); border-left-color: var(--accent); }

  figure { margin: 2em 0 0; }
  figure .ph { aspect-ratio: 16/9; border-radius: var(--radius); }
  figcaption { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 10px; }

  .arch { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 10px; margin-top: 1.5em; }
  .arch .step { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 16px; position: relative; background: var(--surface); }
  .arch .step .k { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .arch .step .t { font-size: 14px; margin-top: 8px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .arch .step:not(:last-child)::after { content:"→"; position: absolute; right: -9px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); color: var(--faint); z-index: 2; }

  .results { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 1.5em; }
  .results .r { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 24px; }
  .results .r b { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2.4rem; display: block; line-height: 1; }
  .results .r span { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); display: block; margin-top: 10px; }
  .results .r small { color: var(--st-active); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; }

  .callout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 20px 22px; border: 1px solid var(--accent-line); background: var(--accent-soft); border-radius: var(--radius); margin-top: 1.5em; }
  .callout .ic { width: 22px; height: 22px; color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .callout p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1rem; }
  .callout strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-ink); margin-bottom: 6px; }

  .next-proj { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--paper-2); }
  .np-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; padding-block: clamp(40px,6vw,72px); }
  .np-inner .t { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem); letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .np-inner .k { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }

  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .case { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-toc { display: none; }
    .case-body { grid-column: 1; max-width: var(--maxw-read); margin-inline: auto; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .meta-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .arch { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .arch .step::after { display: none; }
    .results { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .np-inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }
</style>
